# Security Rules

## Secrets

### MUST

- [ ] Load secrets only from environment / GitHub Actions secrets
- [ ] Document new env vars in `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md` and `.env.example`
- [ ] Route config through `src/config/config.ts`

### MUST NOT

- ❌ Hardcode API keys, tokens, passwords, or AWS credentials
- ❌ Commit `.env` files
- ❌ Log credentials, tokens, or sensitive payloads

## Logging

- Use bunyan logger only
- Strip secrets from logged objects
- Prefer identifiers (state code, job id) over raw personal data

## IAM & Network

- Least privilege for ECS task roles
- No unnecessary public exposure of resources
- Security group / IAM expansions require human review

## Dependencies

- New npm packages require human approval
- Prefer well-maintained packages with clear licenses
- Run audits when adding or upgrading dependencies

## Escalation

Security-sensitive changes always require human review before merge.
